# sgi-tess.config - this site's settings for Tess.
#
# Copy to sgi-tess.config at the top of the tree, or let scripts/tess-setup
# write one for you. Every machine reads the same file over the share, so it
# is set once for the whole cluster. tess-ui and tess-preflight find it from
# where they are installed; switches on their command lines still win.
#
# One setting per line: a key, then its value. "#" starts a comment.

# The shared tree: the same path on every machine, where each machine's
# build/<arch> directory is. Leave it out and the tree is wherever this file
# is.
tree      /cluster/dev/sgi-tess

# The machines in the cluster, by the names Array Services uses. tess-ui
# offers these in its Cluster pane, and puts the machine it runs on first,
# because the master runs there. Leave it out to use every machine in the
# array, from "ainfo machines".
hosts     lucy arthur aurora

# The Array Services array they are in, as "ainfo arrays" names it. Leave it
# out to use the default array.
array     42718

# The loopback port the master listens on for tess-ui.
port      7333

# Where Save writes images. Leave it out for the directory tess-ui started in.
# savedir   /cluster/images

# Addresses, for tess-setup only: when a machine cannot resolve one of the
# hosts, tess-setup -apply offers to add this line to its /etc/hosts. Plain
# names, as Array Services and mpirun use them.
# address   lucy    192.0.2.8
# address   arthur  192.0.2.17
# address   aurora  192.0.2.16
